is not my native language. Let me try to explain.\r\n\r\nIn `_instance_unpair` if I skip the unpairing when both masks does **not** match, like the code bellow, the reflection probe will not unpair with the geometry when needed, causing the bug in the picture above where disabling the Reflection Mask does not stop reflections in the geometry:\r\n```\r\nif (!(A->layer_mask & RSG::light_storage->reflection_probe_get_reflection_mask(B->base))) {\r\n\t// Early return if the object's layer mask doesn't match the reflection mask.\r\n\treturn;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I flip the logic and skip the unpairing when both masks **does** match, like the code bellow (current PR code), I suspect that the geometry and probe will not be unpaired even when the visibility is set to false, causing performance decrease since the probe will still be updating the invisible geometry:\r\n```\r\nif ((A->layer_mask & RSG::light_storage->reflection_probe_get_reflection_mask(B->base))) {\r\n\t// Early return if the object's layer mask matches the reflection mask.\r\n\treturn;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf this is true, I believe that for reflection probes is better to not skip the unpairing in `_instance_unpair`.","created_at":"2025-05-15T17:05:16Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T17:05:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106411#discussion_r2091632330","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106411","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2091632330"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106411#discussion_r2091632330"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106411"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2091632330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":215,"original_line":2